<id/18/1885/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Dry Goods manufactured"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_woven_fabrics_apparel/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a commercial name for textile fabrics, cottons, woollens, laces, hard-wares, and some few other articles; in contradistinction to groceries. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 146]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_woven_fabrics_apparel): Textile manufactures (jute, silk broad stuffs, hair cloth, felt, dry goods, sails) belong with Woven Textiles, not paper/glass/sundries. Layer-1 observations: 4 rows, 1875–1875. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×4. Units: (no unit) ×4. Top routes: Quebec → United States ×1; Quebec → Newfoundland ×1; Quebec → All Countries ×1; Quebec → Great Britain ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1885" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dry Goods manufactured"@en ;
